    "body": "Triage, checked on `main` 8b0d784.\n\n**How a machine is added today** (the #170 path, see `docs/decisions/170-tormach-machines.md`):\n- One `.mch` JSON file in `assets/machines/`, with `general` (model, vendor, kind), `kinematics` (units, axes and travels, rotaries, spindle with `ranges` and `rigid_tapping`) and `controller`. The figures come from the machine's own operator's manual. The decision record cites the manual numbers (UM10586 and so on) rather than storing the manual, which keeps vendor documents out of the repo.\n- An entry in `posting::MACHINES` and in the `every_shipped_machine_mounts_and_speaks_its_declaration` test (`crates/app/tests/machine.rs`).\n- A post: one of the `.cps` scripts in `assets/posts/` (`posting::BUILTINS`). A new controller dialect is a new script.\n\n**Gaps against the list in this issue:**\n- No place in the app to create or validate a machine. #287 (Machine configurations pane) covers that.\n- No written onboarding checklist. The steps above live only in #170's decision record. A short `docs/` page would answer \"what info do we need\", and fits #291's documentation site.\n- No standard validation job. `testdata/models/Milling-test.step` (a D-shaped plate with a blind bore) is already used by several suites and could carry face, contour, pocket, chamfer, drill, bore and tap. Driven headless through `camcraft-cli mcp` (import, stock, tools, operations, generate, verify, post), it gives a program to dry-run on the machine. Nothing like that exists yet for turning.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
